  "result": "Perfect! All 314 tests pass (including 43 new currency tests). Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/money.js`** \u2014 Extended with foreign currency support\n\n**New exports:**\n\n1. **`RATES`** \u2014 Exchange rates object:\n   - `EUR: 1` (baseline)\n   - `USD: 1.085` (units of USD per EUR)\n   - `GBP: 0.8425` (units of GBP per EUR)\n\n2. **`convert(cents, currency)`** function:\n   - Converts amount from EUR cents to target currency\n   - Takes EUR cents and currency code (EUR, USD, or GBP)\n   - Returns `ok({ value: converted_cents })` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n   - Uses banker's rounding for precise calculations\n   - Handles negative amounts correctly\n   - Example: `convert(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 `{ ok: true, value: 10850 }`\n\n3. **`formatMoney(cents, currency)`** function:\n   - Formats amount in any currency with proper symbol\n   - Takes amount in that currency's cents\n   - Returns formatted string with:\n     - Currency symbol: `$` (USD), `\u00a3` (GBP), `\u20ac` (EUR)\n     - Thousands separators\n     - 2 decimal places\n   - Example: `formatMoney(123456, 'USD')` \u2192 `\"$1,234.56\"`\n\n**`src/errors.js`** \u2014 Updated:\n- Added `UNKNOWN_CURRENCY` error code with message\n\n**`test/money-currency.test.js`** \u2014 43 comprehensive tests covering:\n- RATES constants and values\n- Currency conversion (all three currencies)\n- Conversion with different amounts (0, 1, 100, large)\n- Rounding behavior (banker's rounding, 0.5 cases)\n- Error handling (unknown currency, case sensitivity)\n- Money formatting (all currencies, negative amounts, large amounts)\n- Round-trip conversions\n- Precision and sign preservation\n- Penny amounts and thousands separators\n- Real invoice total conversions\n\nAll 314 tests pass successfully (271 previous + 43 currency).",
